    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (81.45) and **Junior Caminero** (67.62). **Yordan Alvarez** is our clear standout, benefiting from a favorable 4.73 xERA matchup and an elite xwOBA of 0.465, while **Junior Caminero** maximizes a +10% park factor adjustment that pushes him well into our strong-start territory. **Lars Nootbaar** also grades out as a primary play at 65.16, thanks to a significant +19% boost derived from the matchup against Feltner and a favorable platoon advantage. While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** carries a solid 58.33, the optimizer penalizes him heavily (-15%) for the platoon disadvantage against a left-handed arm, though his top-of-the-order positioning keeps him marginally viable for those needing high-floor volume.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves the utility slot and our secondary options. **Nelson Velazquez** technically graded out as a bench piece due to his exclusion from the official starting lineup; however, his underlying metrics against Houser were strong enough that he would have challenged for an OF spot had he been penciled in. Our pursuit of the scarce SB category remains a strategic focal point; while **Trea Turner** (59.89) is hindered by a high-hold pitcher who discourages base running, his daily floor is too high to bench. Conversely, **Caleb Durbin** (54.26) and **Chase Meidroth** (52.00) provide necessary stability, though they must navigate matchups that aren't overly favorable. We are holding **Christian Yelich**, **Colt Keith**, and **Casey Schmitt** inactive, with **Casey Schmitt** specifically flagged for IL status, ensuring we don't bleed plate appearances while chasing category gains. Be mindful of the Leahy start against **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber**; despite their solid scores, Leahy\u2019s propensity to stifle runners could limit our ceiling in the stolen base column today.",
